# Rocq/Coq build artifacts
proofs/*.vo
proofs/*.vok
proofs/*.vos
proofs/*.glob
proofs/.*.aux

# Machine-specific hardware probe cache. NEVER commit this: it carries one
# card's GPU_NAME, SM_VERSION and SM_COUNT, and `check_or_probe_hardware`
# skips the probe whenever the file exists -- so a committed profile makes a
# fresh clone on a DIFFERENT card emit PTX targeting the committer's card.
# That is a hard load failure on anything older ("SM version specified by
# .target is higher than default SM version assumed").
.ysu_hw_profile

# The Solidity verifier gate needs `solc`. package.json/package-lock.json are
# tracked so `npm ci` reproduces the exact compiler; node_modules is not.
node_modules/

# Rocq/Coq build artifacts. `tests/proofs_are_checked.rs` compiles in a temp
# directory precisely so these never appear here, but running `coqc` by hand -
# which the proof headers tell you to do - drops them beside the source.
proofs/*.vo
proofs/*.vok
proofs/*.vos
proofs/*.glob
proofs/.*.aux
proofs/.lia.cache
proofs/.nra.cache
proofs/.nia.cache

# ptxas translation validator: everything it can regenerate.
# `tools/ptxas_tval/build_corpus.sh` rebuilds corpus/ and o1/ from the repo's
# own committed tests/*.ptx via ptxas + nvdisasm -- all 67 byte-identically to
# the ones the published results were measured on. A .cubin is a
# machine-specific ELF and a .sass is a disassembly of one; committing either
# is the same mistake as committing .ysu_hw_profile. The *_base.tgz files are
# per-run baselines the mutation harnesses snapshot with mkbase.sh.
tools/ptxas_tval/corpus/
tools/ptxas_tval/o1/
tools/ptxas_tval/*.tgz
# a hand-built fixture's .ptx and .sass are tracked (see fma/); the .cubin it
# passes through is machine-specific and derived, like every other one here.
tools/ptxas_tval/**/*.cubin

# Emitted certificates. One `.v` per compilation that substitutes an exact
# kernel, written beside the artifact it certifies. They are GENERATED and must
# never be committed: a checked-in certificate is the third staleness class this
# repository already names -- an artifact no run of the compiler need reproduce,
# which then reads as a claim about code that has moved underneath it.
*_certificate.v
*_certificate_[0-9]*.v
